name: Immutable context comparison, activation, restore and explicit mirror adoption
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: threats models
require-live-snap: 20 THREAT MODEL LINEAGES | lineages
ask: Can the operator distinguish the active Beta context from the original Alpha and inactive reviewed copy, with explicit activation and history actions?
paste-file: @ART/diff-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART compared
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 20 Application owner | compared-text
expect: context text: 3 change(s)
expect: Reviewed overview α
ask: Does comparison show actual before/after overview, component purpose and question answer, disclose preview limits, and leave active context and immutable objects unchanged?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: diff-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: diff-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: diff-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: diff-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: diff-40x12
keys: PPage PPage
live-snap: diff-paged-40x12
ask: Are the comparison, full-message route and paging usable across the viewport matrix without claiming context equivalence or finding validity?
resize: 120x36
paste-file: @ART/activate-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 result activated | activated
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART activated
paste-file: @ART/restore-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 result restored | restored
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restored
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART edit-mirror
paste-file: @ART/adopt-command.txt
keys: Enter
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 result adopted mirror edits | adopted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART adopted
ask: Do explicit activation, restore and adopt preserve the original objects, append honest history, complete without replacing Map and keep exact context reads independent of the active pointer?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | no-color-ready
submit: threats models
require-live-snap: 20 THREAT MODEL LINEAGES | no-color-lineages
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_lifecycle.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does restart retain the adopted active revision and exact inactive copy, with unchanged source and no provider, scanner or repeated work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
